  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Thung Thrakrek is a broad-finned orca war-leader of the Incursion era, known primarily for his raids on the Nightshelf tunnel-settlement ☽'scar Ramtatus~ and his long combat partnership with Gnarkzund Zaith, a fellow orca raider killed at Aurora Stack. His reputation among the pods — they called him *Thung-the-Remembered* — rests on a kill-count that is, by any honest reckoning, exceptional. That they no longer use the epithet to his face suggests either fear or the recognition that legend is a designation more comfortable when applied posthumously.
    
    He bears extensive damage. His left flank carries the silver scar left by Lucatransiius Glow-bringer, an Aurora Stack defender whose spear-work never healed cleanly; the wound weeps in cold currents and impairs his turning. His left eye clouded after the Shelf campaign — whether from magic exposure or trauma, Thung has not said, and I have noted elsewhere the evidentiary problems with treating his reticence as testimony. His teeth are notched from channeling Threk's Opening, a pressure-depth war-ritual that turns bone into a conduit for deep-current force. His dorsal fin is split three times in ritual scarification, marking three awakenings: Threk Boneday, Slaughter Moon, and a third he refuses to name. Penguin beaks hang from his shoulder-harness, each notched with a date. He still commands through ritual authority and accumulated kills, but his flippers shake when he believes himself unobserved.
    
    ## The Dagger and the Nightshelf
    
    Thung stole the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a fire-core shadow-steel blade of Clever Ice Age provenance, from the Nightshelf — a theft the Nightshelf measured in tunnels permanently lost. The mystic Iarlocias the Silent later recovered it. Thung still references the blade in blood-rituals as though he holds it. His other ritual practices involved pressing crushed aurora-crystal, stolen from the outer spires of the Aurora settlement Light Ingjeizhi, into self-inflicted wounds — aurora-light glowing in the cuts. During the Threk Boneday ritual, he placed the final bone in the spiral arrangement himself, a detail preserved in the interrogation of initiate Kzund-threk-zaith by Gork Slaughterend, Thung's own instructor in the Grend Blood-Arts.
    
    ## Combat Record and Gnarkzund Zaith
    
    At the Dawn Terrace engagement, Thung fought alongside Gnarkzund Zaith with the coordination of long partnership — echoing flick-commands, reading structural weaknesses. When the Grulkzul Omega Strike decompression struck, Gnarkzund Zaith shoved Thung clear. Thung survived. He afterward circled the water where Gnarkzund Zaith had been.
    
    Thung later directed the orca assault on ☽'slew Ravium~, a Nightshelf warren, from the breach point — his damaged flank dragging, his hunt-song commands precise regardless. When Gnarkzund Zaith fell in the main cavern to the ☽'micseleia' Dagger's power, Thung's hunt-songs ceased. He taught Gnarkzund Zaith the collective blood-technique Khrrak's Collapse before an unspecified breach between them; afterward they raided the same targets from different waters without coordinating.
    
    ## Scholarly Significance
    
    Thung provided testimony on the Shattered-Spire Assault under Vestigium∴moria protocols — the sole orca account of the Grulkzul Omega Strike's effects, describing pod-bonds severing audibly, each at a distinct frequency. Qingqe'frostlings field scholars observed him during the ☽'slew Ravium~ engagement, cataloguing his scarification patterns as primary evidence for Rupture-Song mechanics. He remains the only living Rupture-Song practitioner examined in the field. His body is, in a sense, an archive — one more legible than most, and no less damaged for having been read.
